# Migration files are content-hashed by api/src/migrate.ts, and the hash is
# stored in schema_migrations to detect edits to already-applied migrations.
#
# This repo runs with core.autocrlf=true and no other line-ending policy, so
# `git ls-files --eol` reports `i/lf w/crlf`: files are LF in the index and
# CRLF in a Windows worktree. Ubuntu CI checks out LF. Without this, a hash
# computed locally could never match one computed in the pipeline, and the
# integrity check would reject every unchanged migration on the first deploy
# after a local one.
#
# The runner ALSO normalises line endings before hashing. Belt and braces:
# this keeps the bytes consistent, that survives anyone cloning with a
# different git configuration.
*.sql text eol=lf
